-- 2026-10-18. Every puppy photo's focus point from the dog detector on Workers AI, so cards,
-- thumbnails and breed photos are cropped around the puppy (Alex approved the framing review,
-- 2026-10-18). Written by ops/measure_photos.py (the photos on Wix) and the same rule in
-- lib/focus.js (the 16 uploaded demo photos in R2, three of which are plain placeholders with no
-- dog and take the middle). The detector says only where a dog sits, never which puppy it is.
-- 237 photos were stored as Wix's own 4:3 copy (.../v1/fill/w_1400,h_1050,al_c,.../file.jpg), which
-- cut off the top and bottom of 47 portrait photos before the site cropped them again. Those point
-- back at the original. One photo Wix no longer serves, on two archived puppies, is left alone.
-- Plain updates by id, so a second run changes nothing. Run once on staging after a backup.
